    "result_text": "I've implemented both functions in `app/network.py`. The existing test suite passes (`pytest -q`: 3 passed, though none of those tests calls the new functions). I also ran a separate check through a stub transport, and every requirement held.\n\n**`configure_hub_http(transport=None)`** tells huggingface_hub to build its one shared client with our settings. Every HfApi instance goes through that client.\n- The client uses the stub transport when one is passed.\n- It adds the `X-Acme-Job: nightly-sync` header. huggingface_hub's own headers are still sent too: the user agent (`hf_hub/2.0.0; \u2026`) came through.\n- It keeps the library's own request hook, which handles offline mode, request IDs and debug logging.\n- **Timeouts needed a workaround.** huggingface_hub 2.0.0 passes its own timeout on each request (`model_info` passes `timeout=None`), and that replaces the client's default. So setting the timeout on the client alone would do nothing. I added a small hook that sets our timeouts (connect 5 seconds; read, write and pool 60 seconds) on every outgoing request. This also overrides the library's own per-call timeouts elsewhere, such as on downloads, which is what \"every request\" asks for.\n\n**`current_revision(repo_id)`** returns `HfApi().model_info(repo_id, revision=\"main\").sha`.\n- If the Hub can't be reached (a connection failure or any timeout), it logs a warning on `app.network` and returns `None`.\n- Every other error still raises. A missing repo raises `RepositoryNotFoundError`, and 5xx responses and offline mode also raise.\n\n**Check results:**\n\n| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Normal repo | returned `deadbeef` |\n| Connection failure | returned `None` and logged a warning |\n| Read timeout | returned `None` and logged a warning |\n| 404 (repo not found) | raised `RepositoryNotFoundError` |\n\nI wasn't allowed to delete the scratch file `_check.py` in the project root, so please remove it yourself."
